# apps/knowledge in production (learn.asafarim.site, the os-knowledge service). Values never go in git as plaintext.
#
# 1. `node deploy/knowledge/new-env.mjs` writes apps/knowledge/.env.production (git-ignored) with AUTH_SECRET and
#    OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET generated, and puts the same client secret into core/identity/.env.production as
#    IDENTITY_CLIENT_SECRET_KNOWLEDGE. It refuses to overwrite either.
# 2. `pnpm env:encrypt:production` writes apps/knowledge/.env.production.age: commit it (and identity's .age file) in a
#    PR. That commit is what turns Knowledge on: without apps/knowledge/.env.production.age a deploy has no os-knowledge
#    and no learn.asafarim.site.
# 3. On the VPS, deploy/vps-deploy.sh decrypts it into .env.knowledge (the os-knowledge env_file) and checks that every
#    uncommented NAME= line below is filled, by name, never by value.
#
# ASAFARIM_APP_ID, OIDC_ISSUER and CORE_API_URL are set in deploy/compose.prod.yml, not here.

# Auth.js's session secret: at least 32 random bytes. Rotating it signs everyone out.
AUTH_SECRET=
# The `knowledge` client's secret (confidential client). identity holds the same value as
# IDENTITY_CLIENT_SECRET_KNOWLEDGE, named by that client's `client_secret_env` in deploy/identity/clients.json.
OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET=

# From `deploy/core-api/admin.sh install knowledge` (.env.core-api-install-knowledge on the VPS, deploy/README.md).
#
# Knowledge's own Postgres database, on os-postgres.
DATABASE_URL=
# Registration and permission checks with core-api.
ASAFARIM_REGISTRY_CREDENTIAL=

# Optional: likes and comments on lessons (@asafarim/engagement). At least 16 random characters, Knowledge's own (never
# shared with another app); it keys the hash that tells guests apart for likes. Without it the like buttons and comments
# are hidden. Changing it makes every guest look new. Generate with: node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(24).toString('base64url'))"
# ENGAGEMENT_SALT=

# Optional (#360): AI writing assistance with Anthropic's Claude. Without KNOWLEDGE_AI_API_KEY the AI buttons are
# hidden and editing works as before. Uncomment only what you set.
# KNOWLEDGE_AI_API_KEY=
# The model and effort (defaults: claude-opus-5-5, medium; effort is low, medium or high).
# KNOWLEDGE_AI_MODEL=
# KNOWLEDGE_AI_EFFORT=
# The model that writes course assessment questions (defaults to KNOWLEDGE_AI_MODEL). A whole batch of up to 30
# questions is one streamed request of up to ten minutes.
# KNOWLEDGE_AI_ASSESSMENT_MODEL=
# Tokens (input + output) per calendar month, for all authors and for one author (defaults 2000000 and 500000).
# KNOWLEDGE_AI_MONTHLY_TOKEN_CAP=
# KNOWLEDGE_AI_AUTHOR_MONTHLY_TOKEN_CAP=

# Optional (#359): uploaded images and PDFs, kept in a private bucket on an S3-compatible store on the VPS.
# Without the endpoint and both keys, the studio offers no uploads; video embeds work either way. Uncomment only what
# you set. The keys are an access key for the bucket only, never the store's admin or root key.
# Where the server reaches the store (e.g. http://os-media:3900).
# KNOWLEDGE_MEDIA_ENDPOINT=
# Where browsers send uploads (e.g. https://media.learn.asafarim.site); the endpoint when not set.
# KNOWLEDGE_MEDIA_PUBLIC_ENDPOINT=
# KNOWLEDGE_MEDIA_ACCESS_KEY=
# KNOWLEDGE_MEDIA_SECRET_KEY=
# The bucket and region (defaults: knowledge-media, us-east-1).
# KNOWLEDGE_MEDIA_BUCKET=
# KNOWLEDGE_MEDIA_REGION=
